{{Quote|The Republic boundary beyond the Mid Rim&mdash;that's imaginary and has been for years. The hyperspace lanes in the Slice that approach Hutt Space get a lot of pirate activity. There's a wide swath where it's gotten too dangerous to operate.|A Regal Voyager [[Unidentified steward (Regal Zephyr)|steward]]|<ref name="The Living Force">''[[The Living Force]]''</ref>}}
'''The Slice''' was an eastward region of [[the galaxy]].<ref name="GEG">''[[Star Wars: The Galactic Explorer's Guide]]''</ref> A colossal wedge-shaped fan of [[star system]]s, it stretched from the [[Core Worlds]] to the [[Outer Rim Territories]],<ref name="The Living Force" /> and consisted of the region between the [[Perlemian Trade Route]] and the [[Corellian Run]] [[super-hyperroute]]s.<ref name="Scarif">{{EncyclopediaCite|Scarif and Other Planets in the Outer Rim}}</ref> It shared borders with [[the Interior]] westward, the [[New Territories]] northward, and the [[Trailing Sectors]] southward.<ref name="GEG" /> During the [[Republic Era]], [[Pirate|piracy]] was rampant in the Slice, leading corporations to relocate from the region. Combined with the [[Jedi Order]] closing a number of [[Jedi outpost]]s in the Slice, the region became even less secure.<ref name="The Living Force" /> By [[33 BBY]],<ref name="TLF Date">{{LivingForceDate}}</ref> five major pirate gangs operated in the Slice: the [[Filthy Credits]], the [[Poisoned Blades]], the [[Riftwalkers]], the [[Staved Skulls]], and the [[Vile]].<ref name="The Living Force" />

{{Stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
''[[Star Wars: The Galactic Explorer's Guide]]'' depicts the Slice in a stylized map that does not match the prior [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] definition, dropping the [[Arrowhead Region]] and excluding a section of the galaxy southeast of [[Corellia]].<ref name="GEG" /> The guide's author [[Jason Fry]] has stated that the map was developed for ease of readability on a mobile phone for use in the Disney parks, and that its borders should not be considered definitive or overriding other sources.<ref name="Fry">{{EmailCite|email=File:AtlasEmail-2025-08-31.png|creator=[[Jason Fry]]|date=2025-08-31}}</ref>

